title The ladder that outran its own page -- STOA334-346 fold home, and a nib padded with a zero
prompt Open as SILENCE under the INNER LOOP Standing block -- roster cold then hot, reds first as standfast, QA on touch, council rota row N mod 5, prose witnesses on prose sends, stamp-and-name, ASCII-first, READ SCOPE -- then pick up the running thread and take the infrastructure lane.
think ListAgents named one peer, grain-96, and I messaged it before touching a file. That was the right call twice over -- HEAD moved under me three times during the lap, 0f00416a5 to 54cda9f2b to fe91b674a to dd4991dbf, so REDS %291's checkout-is-single-writer reading was live the whole round.
think The rota computed row 0. N is git rev-list --count HEAD at 3650, and 3650 mod 5 is 0. My previous lap read row 3, so this advances by exactly one and no hand advance was owed. Aether, Jupiter, why the work exists, sense of hearing. Its threshold page names the fixed pair sound/silence -- a green witness is sound, and a claim retired because it could no longer be checked is an honest silence, and the lap records both. This lap did exactly one of each.
think The cold roster took 28 minutes and closed guards_run=80, guards_green=76, guards_red=4, tree_at_close=1aa6dc065195, tree_moved=yes. The tail-60 pipe showed one red by name; the other three were read from construction/standing-equipment-reds/, which is where the runner puts its evidence. Four reds, and sorting them by owner is the whole of the triage.
think construction/ITINERARY.md line 58 read **Git nib:** `138cabf1b0`, and git rev-parse answers "unknown revision" -- the hash resolves to NOTHING. The real commit is 138cabf1bf14941b9a8ec9152d6437854f851a6e, so `git rev-parse --short=10 HEAD` gives `138cabf1bf`. Somebody read the 9-character form off `git log --oneline` and padded it to ten with a zero. git blame names e13289fb5, my own previous lap's card commit, so this is my red and I own it.
think Two rostered guards red on that one line and they are one root wearing two names -- remember_git_nib refuses because the nib names no commit in this repository, and nib_honesty prints advertised=1 gone=1 verdict=FLOATING_CLAIM. The remember-git-nib witness's own header names two honest states and no third; a hash that resolves to nothing is the third, and it caught it.
think The other two reds are the peer's moving tree rather than faults of mine to chase. readme_metrics.rish check and geode_libraries.rish check both exit 0 on the settled tree while their witnesses red, and tools/fixtures/readme_metrics_check.sh reads drift=3 -- Fascia 64 on the page against 54 fresh, Witnesses 1724 against 1725, rooms-past-listing 2 against 1. tools/hooks/pre-commit regenerates that block at the next commit, so repairing it under a hand committing every few minutes is %291 in a different hat. Named to the peer, left alone.
think The lane's next door was already written down. active-designing/20260827-174816 orders the Glow work Lindy-first and its item 2 reads "the ladder folds its thirteen rungs home"; the charter calls that lap one still looking for its owner, and docs/STOA.md says the same on its own face. My previous lap closed item 1. This is the crux of what is left that no gate holds.
think Two faults in one page, and they pull against each other. docs/STOA.md stood at 180 lines while its H1 declared <=80, and its last row read STOA333 while thirteen further rungs stood green in tools/g/ witnesses. Folding thirteen rows in makes the page longer. The resolution is that a compressor compresses: the page already carried eight range rows and then degenerated into 159 one-per-rung rows, 51 of which recorded a lean rather than a claim.
think tools/fixtures/declared_ceiling_scan.sh reads the H1 title only when no `**Ceiling:**` header exists, at line 213, and its own error text at line 256 names the remedy -- write it '**Ceiling:** <=N lines'. So seating the header form is what the guard asks for rather than a dodge of it, and ZETA, LULU, and TUBE already carry exactly that line. The catch is that the header moves the page from a ratchet into a hard gate: `over` exits 1 above zero at line 368, so the header and the compression had to land in one edit or the guard reds.
think Every one of the thirteen claims was read rather than invented. STOA334-337 live as /// comments in glow/lower_shop_gate.rye; 338a, 338b, 339, 339b, 340, 341, 346 name their rung in their witness's first line; 342-345 are the first lines of their own gate-*.glow desks. Landing stamps came from git, and the file's elder name is why the first search missed -- `git log -S` on glow/lower_shop_gate.rye found nothing before 20260826 because the file was glow/lower_bartis.rye until it was renamed.
think Author dates and committer dates disagree, and the committer dates are the honest ones. STOA342's author date reads 20260804.043333, which would place it after 345, while its committer date reads 003744 and sits correctly between 341 and 343. All thirteen committer stamps run monotone, so the page uses those and says so. The one apparent inversion left is 338b below 339, and that is the order the work actually took -- the STOA339 commit body says "338b waits under the rune grant" in its own words.
obs The QA card graded the page A both before and after -- 94 then 96 at meter, service 75 then 85. That reading is worth keeping honestly: an A page can still be a stale ladder. The card measures Register, Reach, Truth, and Service, and none of those four asks whether a census page holds the rows the tree actually ran. The grade was right and the page was wrong, and both statements stand.
obs The style sweep paid for itself and I would have shipped without it. The first draft measured 45% negative sentences against the 14% the page had before, because I had written "is not a thing a reader needs", "Nothing here is invented", and "worse than one that says where the rows are" -- that last one is the compare-by-decay construction Gauge seated against on 20260823.201533, in a guide that names the trap. Rewriting three sentences took the reading to 18%, inside even the Door ceiling, with every claim held.
obs The ratchet wants to fall and I left it standing on purpose. pages_grade_only measures 0 now against grade_only_ceiling=1, and the discipline is that a ceiling only ever falls; lowering it to 0 would make a new title-grade declaration red on the lap it arrives. The line lives in tools/fixtures/declared_ceiling_scan.sh, which the peer rewrote this afternoon for %295's exemption, and I had already told them in writing I would stay out of tools/. Keeping that word is worth more than the one-line fall, so it is the round's one recommendation instead.
obs The full hot roster did not run, and the reason is a measurement rather than a preference. The cold pass took 28 minutes and the peer landed four commits inside it; a hot pass would refuse under tree_moved for the same reason, and staged work waiting 28 minutes for that refusal is exactly what a peer's fleet_round_open stashes. I ran the scoped set the sync rota sanctions -- the guards whose watched files intersect this round's paths -- and committed promptly instead.
obs No REDS row booked for the nib. The seam already has one: the remember-git-nib witness's own header names REDS %103 as where this lived "and where it returned", and %255 seated the empty-index check that governs the amend. A third row for the same seam would be a lantern where a loom already stands; what was missing was not a rule but a correct ten characters.
