file session-logs/date/20260828/20260828-201439_the-ladder-that-outran-its-own-page.kyri this record
recommend check-in (Claude) -- three seats want a word and none is mine to take. First, grade_only_ceiling falls 1 to 0 in tools/fixtures/declared_ceiling_scan.sh, a one-line ratchet fall I am holding because I gave the peer my word to stay out of tools/ this round; it is theirs to take or mine on their say-so. Second, README.md's metrics block reads drift=3 against a fresh measurement and geode-libraries has drifted with it -- both regenerate at the next commit through tools/hooks/pre-commit, so they close themselves or they are a red nobody has named. Third, the lane's charter item 3 is the rooms taking their own words with glow/gen/ folding by letter, and that one is a compiler change rather than a git mv: glow/glow_run.rye builds its import path as the flat format string "glow/gen/{s}.glow" at lines 166 and 241, so the fold needs its own witnesses and its own lap.
obs Added at round close, after the send. The two reds I handed to the peer as theirs are mine, and measurement said so. README.md's block and the tree agreed at `63276d9ab` (page 1724, `git ls-tree` 1724) and diverged at `138cabf1b` (page 1724, tree 1725) -- my own previous lap's commit, the one that added `tools/g/glow_choir_witness.rish`. It has stood diverged across four peer commits since. The row that moved is the witness count, which is the one row `tools/hooks/pre-commit` exists to keep; the scan's own comment already says fascia and rooms-over drift from commits that move neither and are caught by the roster instead, so those two are the design working rather than a gap.
obs The mechanism, proven in a throwaway pen both directions. `tools/hooks/pre-commit` line 112 reads its trigger from the STAGED set -- `git diff --cached --name-only --diff-filter=AD -- 'tools/*_witness.rish' '*.rye'`. A pen with one staged witness prints it; the same command during `git commit --amend` prints nothing, because the index equals the commit being amended; a freshly staged witness prints again, which proves the pathspec itself still reaches the folded `tools/g/` room and the blindness is the amend rather than the fold. My previous lap committed `138cabf1b` with `--no-verify` and then redid it as `--amend --no-edit`, so the one invocation that could have refreshed the page never ran and the one that ran could not see.
obs A second finding, independent of the first and worse for being quiet. `tools/r/readme_metrics.rish` line 61 reads `if mode != "write" then exit exit-ok`, so `check` renders the block and returns success WITHOUT ever comparing it against the page. That is why `readme_metrics.rish check` exits 0 while `tools/fixtures/readme_metrics_check.sh` reads `drift=3` on the same bytes. The rostered witness is honest because it calls the scan directly; the driver's own subcommand named `check` is a check in name only, and anybody reaching for the obvious one gets told the page is fine.
obs I did not repair README.md, and the reason is a measurement taken at round close rather than the promise I made earlier. `git status` shows the peer staging `tools/w/waymark_rung_drift_witness.rish` -- a new witness file, which is exactly the trigger, so their next commit refreshes both pages by the designed path. My write would have raced a repair already inbound and gone stale on their commit, since the count moves 1725 to 1726 as they land. Surfaced rather than crossed.
obs No REDS row booked, and this one is a custody fact rather than a preference. `construction/REDS.md` is modified UNSTAGED in the worktree -- the peer is mid-write on `%329` (`20260828.202405`) with its fold archive untracked beside it. Appending my row to that file would put my text in a file holding their uncommitted row, and committing it would sweep their row into my commit. So the row is written out in full to them instead, three fields ready to place, and the number waits for `git fetch xy` under fetch-before-book.
obs My own red, owned plainly and the worst of the lap. Repinning the nib after the log accretion, I read HEAD, then ran `git commit --amend` -- and between those two commands the peer landed three commits, so the amend landed on THEIR commit `bd72bc0ff` ("session-logs: the counter and the window") rather than on mine, folding my one ITINERARY nib line into their round as `409dfbda0`. Nothing of theirs was lost: `git diff bd72bc0ff 409dfbda0 --stat` reads one file, one insertion, one deletion, and both their files stand inside the published commit. The blemish is provenance -- their commit body never mentions a nib line it now carries.
obs It is NOT repaired by rewriting, and that is the law rather than a preference. `409dfbda0` is already on `xy/main`, so undoing it means a force-push of published history, which is custody gate %5 and Keaton's explicit word. The forward repair is a plain commit that repins the card to `409dfbda0` itself -- a commit that lives on the remote, so it resolves in a fresh clone, which the pre-amend sibling `bd72bc0ffd` would not.
obs The lesson is exact and it is REDS %291 one turn tighter than the row states it. The row says a checkout is a single-writer resource and `git status` names paths rather than hands. This lap adds that `git commit --amend` reads HEAD at the instant it runs, not at the instant you decided to amend, so on a shared checkout the amend has no target -- it has whatever arrived. The empty-index check from %255 passed cleanly here and could not help, because the index was genuinely empty; what was occupied was the branch. A safe amend on a shared checkout needs the hash it intends -- `git commit --amend` against a captured HEAD, refused when HEAD has moved -- and this tree has no such guard today.
obs A second look corrected a first, in public. I read `declared_ceiling` and `remember_git_nib` as RED in the same pass; `declared_ceiling` re-runs at exit 0 with `control_pass=57 control_fail=0`, so that reading was my own race against the peer's mid-write tree rather than a fault. Only the nib was real.
